{
 "metadata": {
  "description": "Stability tests of the Lustre 2.17.0 cluster (RDMA/o2ib, FLR), performed 2026-10-01 after the cluster had been powered off for about 3 months. Source of truth: UJEP-LAB/benchmarks/stability (CSVs, logs), tooling UJEP-LAB/tools/stability.py.",
  "cluster": "10 nodes: 2 heads (MGS+MDT0 on Head-1, MDT1 on Head-2) + 8 computes (16 OSTs)",
  "kernel": "5.14.0-611.13.1_lustre.el9.x86_64 (Rocky Linux 9.7)",
  "units": "seconds unless noted; times relative to the first IPMI power-on command",
  "scripts": {
   "legacy": "lustre-startup with iteration-counted timeouts: real MGS wait limit about 145-170 s, LNET wait about 11 s, no retry",
   "fixed": "lustre-startup with $SECONDS wall-clock deadlines (MGS 600 s, LNET 120 s) and Restart=on-failure (deployed between the 16:15 and 16:38 runs)"
  },
  "caveats": [
   "Cold boots were done as a small number of runs (4 graceful with the fixed script, 1 at 240 s Head-1 delay); not statistics.",
   "Per-node times use node clocks corrected against the controller (+-1-2 s).",
   "Restart=on-failure retry path was not exercised (skipped, 600 s Head-1 delay test).",
   "Hard power-off results are not representative of production: the cluster runs on two power lines with two UPS each and scheduled shutdowns."
  ]
 },
